{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04WT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$j : \\mathcal{C}/U \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0007": "$j_!p : j_!\\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$j_!\\mathcal{S} = \\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0009": "$j_!p : j_!\\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$j \\circ p$", "MATH_0011": "$h_U$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "MATH_0013": "$$\nj_!\\mathcal{S} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{C}/U\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$p$", "MATH_0015": "$1$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0017": "$q : \\mathcal{T} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0019": "$p : \\mathcal{T} \\to \\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0021": "$p : \\mathcal{T} \\to \\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0008": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0009": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf ", "TEXTBFOPEN_0002": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a7000bb71be1e4c2e4a4b97e98f7ff29666a395dfdcd36cc3a195c91d291fd8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:145c35aa312120a0eec61b610ce89243f8c9c432ecb33bb63d24b34007de872b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAssume that <MATH_0001> is a site,\nand <MATH_0002> is an object of <MATH_0003> whose associated representable\npresheaf is a sheaf. We denote <MATH_0004>\nthe localization functor.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0001>Construction A.<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> Let <MATH_0005> be a stack\nover the site <MATH_0006>. We define a stack\n<MATH_0007> as follows:\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<STRUCT_0005> As a category <MATH_0008>, and\n<STRUCT_0006> the functor <MATH_0009>\nis just the composition <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0007>\nWe omit the verification that this is a stack (hint: Use that\n<MATH_0011> is a sheaf to glue morphisms to <MATH_0012>). There is a canonical\nfunctor\n<MATH_0013>\nnamely the functor <MATH_0014> which is a <MATH_0015>-morphism of stacks over <MATH_0016>.\n\n<STRUCT_0008><STRUCT_0009>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0002>Construction B.<TEXTBFCLOSE_0002>\nLet <MATH_0017> be a stack over <MATH_0018>\nwhich is endowed with a morphism of stacks <MATH_0019>\nover <MATH_0020>. In this case it is automatically the case that\n<MATH_0021> is a stack over <MATH_0022>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:660c248838897d18aee730820ae66e28709fccdceeb8874b8a016a389dc81ea8", "unit_id": "tag:04WT:prose-0002"}
